+/**
+ * Wide picture, for a game that only knows how to draw a 4:3 picture. With AURORA_VIEWPORT_STRETCH the
+ * frame takes the shape of the window, which stretches that picture sideways. Wide picture undoes the
+ * stretch: the 3D scene shows more to the left and right instead (the camera opens up, nothing gets
+ * fatter), and what the game draws flat on the screen - its clock, its text boxes - keeps its shape in
+ * the middle. Draws that cover the whole frame, like a fade to black, still reach both sides.
+ *
+ * gameAspect is the shape the game draws its picture for (4.0f / 3.0f); 0 turns wide picture off.
+ */
+void AuroraSetWidePicture(float gameAspect);
